  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Calculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $5{y}^{2}-16{x}^{2}=36$ intersects the line $y=-2x.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=-2x,$ we first replace $y$ with $-2x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}-16{x}^{2} & =36 \\\\ 5(-2x)^{2}-16{x}^{2} & =36 \\\\ 5(4{x}^{2})-16{x}^{2} & =36 \\\\ 20{x}^{2}-16{x}^{2} & =36 \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & =36 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9 \\\\ x & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
